    # v406 (02/11/2026) -- THE CLOSURE: 301 new modules in the kernel (the 300 of the ChatGPT bench, recompiled from source, and the candidate CanonicalFullTGLWitnessR1); the Fock certificate inhabited by construction and the passage to the continuum READ from the kernel of the rite; the four witness keys stop being literal; the reservations stated. Numbers come from the core of this rite, never typed.
    # The top box (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule does not move. Nothing here moves the gate. Kernel validity is not creditation.
    _rg406 = ("fechamento_v406", "cunhagens_v406", "kh_n1_cobertura_v406")
    _ok406 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in _rg406)
    _f406 = core.get("fechamento_v406") or {}
    _v406 = _f406.get("values") or {}
    _ch406 = _f406.get("four_keys") or {}
    _el406 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cvr406 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _ev406 = ((globals().get("_V406_FECHO_CONTRACT") or {}).get("bundle") or {}).get("eval_removidos") or {}
    _i406 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _b406 = lambda x_: (r"\textsf{True}" if x_ is True else r"\textsf{False}" if x_ is False else r"\text{n/a}")
    _tx406 = lambda x_: "n/a" if x_ is None else str(x_).replace(chr(92), "").replace("_", r"\_\allowbreak{}")
    s.append(r"\section*{The closure: the passage to the continuum and the inhabited certificate}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The closure: the passage to the continuum and the inhabited certificate}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the v406 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok406 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The order.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 02/11/2026 (our translation; the Portuguese is the quotation): we must build everything, because we can no longer lose the logical order, it is the closure; and the priority: the construction of the passage to the continuum is what matters most. "
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} " + _i406(_v406.get("n_modulos")) + r" new modules in the kernel, under \texttt{TGLExt/F1Fecho394}: the 300 of the ChatGPT bench (mission F1.FECHO\_20261015, 15 and 16/10/2026), recompiled from source in the R3 integration of 02/11 (300 compiled, 0 failures; each source checked by sha256 against the bench receipt before the normalisation: the imports became \texttt{TGLExt.F1Fecho394.*} and " + _i406(_ev406.get("blocos")) + r" instrumentation \texttt{\#eval} blocks (\texttt{IO.println}, \texttt{IO.FS.withFile}) were removed from " + _i406(_ev406.get("modulos")) + r" modules, none inside a proof; the header of those modules dates from their writing, with the label \texttt{UNCOMPILED CANDIDATE}: the compilation that counts is the receipt of 16/10, the integration and the rite), and the candidate \texttt{CanonicalFullTGLWitnessR1}, a provisional name given by the management. "
             + _i406(_v406.get("n_flags")) + r" flags, named declarations only; the kernel ladder closes at " + _i406(_el406.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i406(_el406.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i406(_cvr406.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i406(_cvr406.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. The v405 stones and records \emph{stay as they are}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The passage to the continuum.} \textsf{[REAL]} The top of the closure (\texttt{CanonicalFockModularCoreInputR1}) inhabits, for every $D:\texttt{CanonicalNetInput}$, the 21 fields of \texttt{RemainingModularCoreInput}\,$D$ (\texttt{modularCoreInput}): the trace of the core is the cyclic trace \texttt{cyclicTraceCandidate}, the supremum of the positive weight over the shift-equivalent positives (\texttt{ShiftRelated}; cyclicity is a property of the relation, the same route already accepted in the kernel for the tower, V354); "
             r"$P_F=\texttt{positiveAsCore}\,(\texttt{add}\ \texttt{leftPositive}\ \texttt{rightPositive})$ has trace $1$ by the dual calibration (\texttt{dual\_calibration}: the unit of the trace is \emph{posted} by the $e^{-s}$ scale of the dual action); the equal halves come from the normalised split (\texttt{normalized\_split\_exists}; $P_F$, $P_+$ and $P_-$ are chosen by \texttt{Classical.choose}, not canonical: the type does not ask for canonicity). "
             r"Over the physical net \texttt{physicalCanonicalNet} ($K:=\texttt{compactPhysicalNet}$; monotonicity, locality, translation, boost and the wedge glue are theorems) sits the certificate \texttt{physicalFockCertificate}, with \texttt{physical\_trace} by \texttt{rfl}. \textsf{[ONTO]} The operator reads (our translation): the absolute One is the light compressed by the ACOM into an absolute ONE; and, of the type~I / type~III pair: there is no bridge to type~I, there is the mirroring of information happening in real time; the management reads in this the dual calibration and the finite inclusions in III$_1$ [KNOWN]; none of these readings is a kernel term.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The canonical term of the witness.} \textsf{[REAL]} The candidate assembles $\texttt{canonicalFullTGLWitness}:=\langle\texttt{lightNet}\ \texttt{physicalFockCertificate},\ \texttt{lightRealization}\ \texttt{physicalFockCertificate}\rangle:\texttt{FullTGLWitness}$ and, through it, \texttt{Nonempty FullTGLWitness}. It is the exact name that the layer \texttt{witness\_layers.canonical\_full\_witness\_term\_constructed} has measured since v367 (name absent $\Rightarrow$ False); in this rite it reads " + _b406(_ch406.get("witness_layers.canonical_full_witness_term_constructed")) + r".")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The four keys, from literal to reading.} \textsf{[REAL]} Since v394 the program carried as the literal \texttt{False} the keys \texttt{rede\_fock\_v394.whole\_certificate\_inhabited}, \texttt{psibit\_v395.conditional\_psion\_face.inhabitant\_exhibited} and \texttt{testemunha\_estatica\_v396.fock\_face.inhabitant\_exhibited}: they recorded the state of that time. Since 16/10/2026 the bench had the inhabitant; the management only read it on 02/11 (erratum E14, in its own name: the sceptic who reads the type and does not read the bench). Where the v395 (\emph{The psibit}), v396 (\emph{The static witness}) and v405 (\emph{The gap, beside}) sections of this paper, and the sealed records of those versions (\texttt{psibit\_v395}, \texttt{testemunha\_estatica\_v396}, \texttt{cunhagens\_v395/v396/v397}, \texttt{gap\_v405}), say in the present tense that the kernel does not inhabit the certificate, read: it was the state of that date; the current reading is this one; the sealed texts stay as record. "
             r"In v406 the three are read from the kernel of the rite itself (\texttt{physicalFockCertificate} in the trio, declared in the top module, source by sha256) and read " + _b406(_ch406.get("rede_fock_v394.whole_certificate_inhabited")) + r", " + _b406(_ch406.get("psibit_v395.conditional_psion_face.inhabitant_exhibited")) + r" and " + _b406(_ch406.get("testemunha_estatica_v396.fock_face.inhabitant_exhibited")) + r"; the status becomes \texttt{" + _tx406(_ch406.get("psibit_v395.conditional_psion_face.status")) + r"}. "
             r"What stays \texttt{False} stays \emph{by theorem}: \texttt{full\_static\_witness\_exists} (the continuous leakage forbids the static closure) reads " + _b406(_ch406.get("qg_closure.gate.full_static_witness_exists")) + r" and \texttt{trivial\_inhabitant\_exists} reads " + _b406(_ch406.get("witness_rigidity.trivial_inhabitant_exists")) + r"; and the lemma that would link \texttt{psion C} to the \texttt{psionCorner} is still missing (\texttt{linked\_to\_the\_corner\_by\_a\_lemma} = " + _b406(_ch406.get("testemunha_estatica_v396.fock_face.linked_to_the_corner_by_a_lemma")) + r").")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The reservations, stated before any use.} \textsf{[OPEN/KNOWN]} $K(O)\neq\bot$ for compact $O$ is not proved: the nontriviality of the net is a theorem only on the wedge (\texttt{physical\_canonical\_net\_nonzero}); the type asks for no more; Reeh--Schlieder stays [KNOWN]. \textsf{[KNOWN/DECLARED]} The phrase ``II$_\infty$ core'' in the docstring of the field $P_F$ is neither proved nor required by the type. \textsf{[REAL, scope]} The trace is ENNReal and cyclic; it is not a linear functional nor additive outside the positive cone. "
             r"\textsf{[DECLARED]} The bench's R7 review was Codex reviewing Codex; the distinct review of 02/11 is by Sonnet (the operator's order), without its own compilation; the independent compilation is this chain's R3 integration and the sandbox build. \textsf{[INPUT]} R4/R5 of the mission (the physical device) remain blocked by the operator and stay out. The name \texttt{CanonicalFullTGLWitnessR1} is provisional: the names of the stones belong to the operator. The day's candidate stones (the friction bridge, the inscribed One, K as the tangent) stay out of the kernel until he names them.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the record checks in this rite.} \textsf{[REAL]} \texttt{fechamento\_v406}: anchors ok " + _i406(_v406.get("n_ancoras_ok")) + r"/8; bundle modules with the pinned sha256 " + _i406(_v406.get("n_modulos_ok")) + r"/" + _i406(_v406.get("n_modulos")) + r"; flags True " + _i406(_v406.get("n_flags_true")) + r"/" + _i406(_v406.get("n_flags")) + r"; certificate inhabited, read from the kernel: " + _b406(_f406.get("certificate_inhabited")) + r"; the gate of this rite carries the same verdict as the sealed v405. Verdict: \texttt{" + _tx406(_f406.get("verdict")) + r"}. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} What changed in the old records is \emph{only what they read}; no sealed text was rewritten (the v395 and v396 texts stay beside as \texttt{reading\_v395} and \texttt{reading\_v396}); the specs that demanded ``false'' received the version (erratum E17). \textsf{[OPEN]} What nature decides still comes from nature: $\beta$ at $5\sigma$; no new data enters here. Kernel validity is not creditation; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never a confirmation; the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
